STOCK OS – Distributed AI-Driven Inventory Operating System

A cloud-native, event-driven platform automating 80% of inventory and operational workflows using real-time systems + AI intelligence

👩‍💻 Authors
Saumya Singh
Trrishaa Balakrishnan

🏆 CodeHer | Exploree TinkerBell

📌 Abstract

STOCK OS is a distributed, real-time inventory operating system designed to solve consistency, synchronization, and prediction challenges in SME supply chains.

Unlike traditional systems that are reactive and eventually consistent, STOCK OS ensures:

Strong consistency at the data layer
Real-time synchronization across all clients
Embedded AI-driven decision making

👉 Goal: Automate ~80% of business operations

❗ Problem Statement

Existing systems suffer from:

Lack of concurrency control → race conditions
No stock reservation → overselling
Delayed synchronization → inconsistent data
No predictive intelligence → reactive workflows
📉 Impact
15–25% revenue loss
30% order delays
40% drop in repeat customers
💡 Solution Overview

A cloud-native, AI-first inventory OS that is:

Real-time
Predictive
Conflict-free
Fully automated
🧠 AI & Intelligence Layer
⚡ Inference Stack
Groq (LLaMA 3) → sub-100ms inference
Sarvam AI → NLP + voice interaction
Time-Series ML Models → forecasting & prediction
📊 AI Capabilities
Demand Forecasting (60–90 day trends)
Stockout Prediction (days-to-stockout)
Anomaly Detection (duplicate orders, abnormal drops)
Smart Procurement (auto PO generation)
Natural Language Queries (role-aware insights)
🔄 Workflow Automation
Raw Material → WIP → Finished Goods → Orders → Dispatch → Delivery
Atomic state transitions
Event-triggered processing (Kafka)
Zero manual re-entry across pipeline
🏗️ System Architecture
🔹 Frontend Layer
React 18 + Vite + Tailwind
Role-based SPAs
Voice Input (Web Speech API)
QR-based inventory actions

UI is stateless — reflects backend state only

🔹 Backend Layer (Control Plane)
FastAPI (async, high throughput)
Centralized business logic:
Stock validation
Conflict detection
Order lifecycle management
JWT Authentication (secure endpoints)
🔹 Event Streaming Layer
Apache Kafka
Handles:
Inventory events
Order lifecycle events
Audit logs

Enables asynchronous, scalable processing

🔹 AI Intelligence Layer
Groq (LLaMA 3)
Sarvam AI
Time-series forecasting models

AI is embedded within workflows, not post-processing

🔹 Data Layer (Source of Truth)
Supabase (PostgreSQL)
ACID Transactions
Row-Level Security (RLS)
Key Features:
Stock reservation system (Available vs Reserved)
Immutable audit logs
Realtime sync (<200ms latency)
🔹 Caching & Performance
Redis
AI response caching
Rate limiting
Session storage
🔐 Consistency & Concurrency Model
Pessimistic locking (stock reservation)
All writes routed via backend
No client-side state mutation
✅ Guarantees:
Zero overselling
No duplicate allocation
Strong consistency under concurrency
🔑 Core Features
Real-time inventory tracking
Conflict-free order processing
Automated procurement system
Role-based access control
Voice + NLP interaction
Immutable audit trails
📊 Impact Metrics
Metric	Improvement
